comment.narrative:
Target Output 1. 1) METT Scorecard: Alatai SNP: >50, Kan-Achuu SNP >50, Sary-Chelek SNR: >65, Padysh-Ata SNR: >50, Besh Aral SNR: >50, Saimaluu-Tash SNP: >40 2) HCVF management approach has legal basis, and relevant regulations are produced; 3) Integration of HCVF management measures in FMPs and level of implementation in Toktogul and Toguz-Toro districts; 4) 1000 hectares patrolled per week in 2021 (baseline * four times the number of anti-poaching ranger team patrols for each location. Assessed as the minimum coverage necessary to ensure effective management, regulatory monitoring, and deterrence of illegal activities)
Target Out II. 1) >40,000 ha Area of sustainably managed forest in Toktogul and Toguz-Toro districts 2) 4,886 ha (500 ha reforestation/afforestation, 4,500 ha supported for natural regeneration) 3) Lifetime indirect GHG emissions avoided - 2,979,548 tons CO2 equivalent 4) e-Pasture Management System implemented by 4 PMCs in Toktogul and Toguz-Toro districts 5) 186,536 ha - SFM in 34,382 ha of HCVF, restore degraded forest in 4,886 ha, and implement SLM in 147,268 ha of pasturelands 6) 147,268 ha of pastureland under SLM in Toktogul and Toguz-Toro districts 7) Number of people whose livelihoods are affected by land degradation in Toktogul and Toguz-Toro districts: - Women: <11,702 - Men: <12,237 - Total: <23,939 - Index: <100% of total population 8) Herder/farmer income change (Women: 10% increase, Men: 10% increase) based on benefits from micro-finance/grant program for individuals participating in the program;
Target Out III. 1) Level of illegal wildlife trade activity, as indicated by number of snow leopard, snow leopard prey, and other illegal wildlife seizures at border crossings and at Manas international airport, as well as number of arrests related to wildlife trafficking: Annual number of seizures: - Snow leopard: <Baseline (at least one seizure assisted by specially trained dogs) - Snow leopard prey: <Baseline (at least one seizure assisted by specially trained dogs) - Other illegal wildlife: <Baseline (at least one seizure by specially trained dogs) - Number of arrests = >baseline - >50% of arrests result in prosecutions 2) International agreement between Kyrgyzstan and at least one bordering country under implementation regarding at least one of the below issues: - Cooperation on law enforcement at border points regarding illegal wildlife trade, - Illegal hunting by border guards, - Data sharing on snow leopard monitoring 3) Publishing of annual estimates with a 60% confidence level (the average confidence level among other snow leopard range states in GSLEP population estimate)
